{#-
  Cisco IOS / IOS-XE -- banners.  **Edit the text below.**

    banner motd ^C
    <text>
    ^C

  `^C` here is two literal characters (caret, C), which is how IOS writes the
  delimiter in the running config. It must not appear in the text itself.

  Blank lines inside the body are content, not layout, so this template is
  rendered with keep_blank_lines. That is why the tags sit at the end of the
  preceding line -- a tag on its own line would add a blank line to the banner.
-#}
{% set mark = delimiter or '^C' %}{% for kind in add %}banner {{ kind }} {{ mark }}{% if kind == 'login' %}

  Authorised access only.

{% else %}

  This system is for the use of authorised users only. Activity on this system
  is monitored and recorded. Anyone using it consents to that monitoring.

  Disconnect immediately if you are not an authorised user.

{% endif %}{{ mark }}
{% endfor %}{% for entry in remove %}no {{ entry.line }}
{% endfor %}
